---
import { projects } from "../../data/projects";
import ProjectLayout from "../../layouts/ProjectLayout.astro";

const project = projects.find((entry) => entry.slug === "mybeli");

if (!project) {
  throw new Error("Missing project data for mybeli");
}
---

<ProjectLayout project={project}>
  <p>
    MyBeli exists to replace a fragile catalog workflow: manually edited PDFs that need to be
    re-exported and resent every time a product, price, or stock count changes.
  </p>

  <h2>What it is for</h2>
  <p>
    The target users are small shop owners who need a current public catalog and a lightweight
    management surface behind it. Instead of treating every client as a separate hand-built site,
    MyBeli is designed as one system serving multiple independent shops.
  </p>

  <h2>What it does</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Publishes a public web catalog that stays current without resending PDFs.</li>
    <li>Provides product and inventory management for each shop owner.</li>
    <li>Supports multiple independent client shops in one platform.</li>
    <li>Allows branded subdomains such as <code>shopname.mybeli.my</code>.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Multi-tenant shape</h2>
  <p>
    The public-safe version of the architecture is straightforward: each shop has its own catalog
    identity, product set, and management workflow, while the application still behaves like one
    shared system. That keeps onboarding and maintenance much simpler than running a custom codebase
    for every client.
  </p>

  <h2>Technical notes</h2>
  <p>
    The only stack detail confirmed here is that the application is built with Elixir. I have
    deliberately left framework specifics, deployment internals, credentials, and customer data out
    of this public page.
  </p>

  <p class="note-box">
    The source repository is private.
  </p>

  <figure>
    <img
      class="frame-image"
      src="/assets/screenshots/mybeli-dashboard.svg"
      alt="Placeholder dashboard panel for MyBeli showing products, stock updates, and catalog publishing."
    />
    <figcaption>
      Placeholder dashboard image. Replace with a redacted real screenshot if a public demo becomes
      available.
    </figcaption>
  </figure>

  <figure>
    <img
      class="frame-image"
      src="/assets/screenshots/mybeli-architecture.svg"
      alt="Placeholder architecture diagram showing branded shop subdomains pointing into a shared multi-tenant application."
    />
    <figcaption>
      Public-safe architecture sketch for the shared multi-tenant model.
    </figcaption>
  </figure>

  <h2>Public links</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Demo: <code>[ADD PUBLIC DEMO URL]</code></li>
    <li>Screenshot set: <code>[ADD SCREENSHOT OR RECORDING LINK]</code></li>
  </ul>
</ProjectLayout>
